WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.918 --> 00:00:03.712
The monster falls.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.005
Olive.

00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:07.340
"We finally slayed the monster."

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:08.925
Water spirit.

00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:10.427
"You did very well."

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.095
Wind spirit.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:15.325
"We must return to the spirit realm."

00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:17.958
Fire spirit. "This is goodbye."

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:20.395
Olive stands frozen.

00:00:23.606 --> 00:00:27.527
Now, how do we get Olive home
from here?

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:31.448
Since her boat sank,
will she take a plane?

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.785
Something a little more imaginative.

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:39.289
She could fly home if she were a bird.

00:00:41.791 --> 00:00:44.502
-What about flying with a parasol?
-You cannot fly with a parasol.

00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:45.754
But you can!

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:49.215
The wind spirit appears before her
one last time and says,

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:51.968
"Olive, open your parasol."

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:56.014
Could you try opening the parasol for me?

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.310
"That parasol is your wings.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.771
You'll be carried away
if you fly too high.

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:06.945
So, step on the ocean's waves,
the river's rocks,

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:09.536
and the fallen leaves on the lake."

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.154
That's a wonderful idea.

00:01:11.654 --> 00:01:15.533
Right? After returning home,
Olive reunites with her father.

00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:21.164
And the first thing she says when they're
reunited after crossing the ocean is...

00:01:21.664 --> 00:01:22.665
What should it be?

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.084
"I'm home."

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.503
No, "Father?"

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.880
Do you have writer's block again?

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:35.428
Could you walk towards me from over there?
I'd like to visualize it.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.597
I can do that.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.434
Across the fallen leaves on the lake
if you can.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.019
Understood.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.607
No, that last bit was just...

00:02:07.377 --> 00:02:08.795
I'm so jealous.

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:12.674
I want to try crossing this lake, too.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:17.387
Do you think I could walk on those leaves?

00:02:20.056 --> 00:02:21.432
One day...

00:02:22.058 --> 00:02:23.852
I promise to show you one day.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:26.229
Okay, Dad?

00:02:30.859 --> 00:02:35.460
How I wish I could hear you call me that
a thousand times more.

00:02:38.264 --> 00:02:39.223
I wish...

00:02:40.119 --> 00:02:42.066
you didn't have to die.

00:02:43.043 --> 00:02:46.547
If only you could have lived...
grown up...

00:02:51.796 --> 00:02:55.592
How I wished that for you.

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:16.613
Did you see that?

00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:21.701
I believe I made three whole steps.

00:03:24.621 --> 00:03:25.455
Sir?

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:27.957
What is the matter?

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.668
Are you feeling ill?

00:03:32.587 --> 00:03:35.465
After granting me this miracle,
I told her,

00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:40.595
"I don't believe there is a God,
but if there were, it would be you."

